From 17ac9e11690b7ba4fd1b44093e9e125d5d3d9490 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "yichen.wang" <yichen.wang@realtek.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 16:46:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gpu: drm: share video overlay planes across CRTCs

Make the video overlay planes a shared pool that any CRTC/mixer can use,
instead of statically binding a fixed set of planes to each CRTC.

 - Create the shared overlay planes once at bind time
   (rtk_crtc_create_additional_planes) with possible_crtcs set to every
   CRTC; on Kent this is V1-V4, other SoCs default to none. Planes start
   unassigned (DISPLAY_INTERFACE_MIXER_NONE) and are routed to a mixer at
   commit time.

 - Program each mixer's layer z-order from the planes' normalized zpos in
   atomic_flush (rtk_crtc_program_mixer_order), resending only when it
   changed. Overlay planes get a mutable zpos property, and the per-layer
   order table is filled through a shared rtk_mixer_order_set_layer()
   helper.

 - Cap the number of planes on a CRTC to what its mixer's hardware
   compositor can blend (MIXER{1,2,3}_MAX_PLANES) in the CRTC
   atomic_check, and expose that limit as a read-only "max_planes" CRTC
   property. Expose each overlay plane's size limits as read-only
   max_width/max_height plane properties (struct rtk_video_plane_caps).

 - Defer a plane's mixer handover in the plane atomic_check until it is
   safe: return -EBUSY while the plane is still committed to another CRTC
   in DRM state, or while the VO firmware still reports it live on a mixer
   (its deferred configureDisplayWindow has not retired yet). The check
   runs only on migration commits, so steady-state frames are unaffected;
   the -EBUSY lets user-space retry or pick a different free plane.

 - Service out-fences for every plane routed to the ISR's mixer, since
   shared overlays live on drm->dev rather than a single CRTC's plane
   list.

 - Enable the OSD4 cursor plane on mixer2 and program its display window
   from a new plane atomic_enable hook so it lands in the same vsync.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: yichen.wang <yichen.wang@realtek.com>
